course: dictionary
lesson: 7847
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can tell which one an author means by reading the words around it. This is context again: the clues are in the sentence.
explain: «A radiator warms the air next to it, which rises and moves round the room.» Here a radiator is a heater, because it warms air and makes a room warm. The car meaning would not fit with rooms and air.
explain: «Your body is like an engine with a radiator: running makes heat, and sweat carries it away.» Here the radiator is the part of an engine that keeps it cool. The word engine is the clue, and the sentence is about cooling down, not heating a room.
fact: A radiator is a flat metal heater, usually under a window, that warms a room when hot water or steam flows through it.
fact: A car radiator is the part at the front of a car engine that keeps the engine cool.
fact: Warm air rises from a radiator, and this moves warm air round the room.
fact: Radiators often sit under windows, because the rising warm air meets the cold air coming off the glass.
fact: A boiler heats water, and a pump sends the hot water round pipes to radiators.
exercise: In «A radiator warms the air next to it, which rises and moves round the room», what is a radiator? | A pipe that carries water to the sink | A kind of window | The part at the front of a car engine | *A flat metal heater that warms a room
exercise: In «Your body is like an engine with a radiator: running makes heat», what is a radiator? | A metal heater under a window | *The part that keeps an engine cool | A tool for drying gloves | A glowing lamp
exercise: In «A radiator warms the air next to it, which rises and moves round the room», which words tell you it is a heater? | which is a tool | next to it and rises | *warms the air and moves round the room | round the car
test: The mechanic checked the radiator because the engine kept overheating. What does radiator mean here? | A glass window | A flat metal heater under a window | *The part at the front of a car engine that keeps it cool | A bag for gloves
test: Grandad turned up the radiator on the cold morning. What does radiator mean here? | A bag for wet gloves | *A flat metal heater that warms the room | A car engine part | A pipe that carries rain
exam: Which sentence uses radiator to mean a car part? | The radiator warmed the cold classroom | *Running makes heat, and the radiator helps the engine stay cool | Warm air rises from the radiator | Gloves dried on the radiator overnight
